@startuml qnx_dispatch_engine_resource_manager_class_diagram
title QNX dispatch engine - resource-manager adapters
hide empty members
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0

namespace score::message_passing {
    class "QnxDispatchEngine" as Engine

    abstract class "QnxDispatchEngine::ResourceManagerServer" as Server {
        + Start(path : const QnxResourcePath&) noexcept : score::cpp::expected_blank<score::os::Error>
        + Stop() noexcept : void
        --
        # engine_ : std::shared_ptr<QnxDispatchEngine>
        - resmgr_id_ : std::int32_t
        --
        # {abstract} ProcessConnect(ctp : resmgr_context_t*, msg : io_open_t*) noexcept : std::int32_t
    }

    abstract class "QnxDispatchEngine::ResourceManagerConnection" as Connection {
        + GetServer() : ResourceManagerServer&
        --
        # rcvid_ : rcvid_t
        # select_event_ : sigevent
        # ping_event_ : sigevent
        --
        - {abstract} ProcessInput(code : std::uint8_t, message : score::cpp::span<const std::uint8_t>) noexcept : bool
        - {abstract} ProcessDisconnect() noexcept : void
        - {abstract} HasSomethingToRead() noexcept : bool
        - {abstract} ProcessReadRequest(ctp : resmgr_context_t*) noexcept : std::int32_t
    }
}

Server --> Engine : retains shared engine_

note bottom of Server
    Private extended_dev_attr_t base embeds native server attributes.
    Start/Stop delegate attachment to the engine.
    The concrete QnxDispatchServer supplies ProcessConnect.
end note

note bottom of Connection
    Private iofunc_ocb_t base provides the native OCB binding.
    GetServer follows that binding, without another shared engine pointer.
    Concrete ServerConnection supplies the private virtual callbacks.
    It owns reply/notification storage outside the engine unit.
end note

@enduml
